# Theme-aware colors

All UI elements (icons, text, backgrounds, tab bars) must be visible in both light and dark color schemes on iOS, Android, and web. Never rely on default/implicit tints.

- Always derive colors from `Colors` in `frontend/src/constants/theme.js` (via `useColorScheme` or the `useTheme` hook), or use `ThemedText`/`ThemedView` with `themeColor`.
- Explicitly set icon tints. Example for native tabs:

```jsx
<NativeTabs
  iconColor={{ default: colors.textSecondary, selected: colors.text }}
  labelStyle={{ color: colors.textSecondary, selected: { color: colors.text } }}>
```

- For standalone icons (Ionicons, SymbolView), pass `color`/`tintColor` from the theme, e.g. `color={isFocused ? colors.text : colors.textSecondary}`.
- After UI changes, sanity-check contrast in both light and dark mode.
